lesson: 109
title: Faces, edges and corners of cubes
stars: 1
explain: A cube has 6 square faces, 12 edges where two faces meet, and 8 corners where three edges meet.
explain: One cube has 6 + 12 + 8 = 26 faces, edges and corners together, so 3 cubes have 3 × 26 = 78.
vars: a=name b=2..9
answer: 26 * b
exercise: {a} has {b} boxes shaped like cubes. How many faces, edges and corners do the boxes have altogether?
exercise: How many faces, edges and corners do {b} cubes have in all?
exercise: {a} builds {b} cubes. {a.He} counts every face, every edge and every corner. What number does {a.he} get?
exercise: There are {b} cube-shaped boxes on a shelf. Add up the faces, the edges and the corners of all of them. What is the total?
exercise: {a} paints each face of {b} cubes, puts a stripe on each edge and a dot on each corner. How many faces, stripes and dots are there together?
test: Count together all the corners, edges and faces of {b} dice. How many is that?
test: {a} makes {b} cubes from straws and clay: a straw for every edge, a ball of clay for every corner and a paper square for every face. How many pieces does {a.he} use?
test: A cube has 6 faces. What is the sum of the edges, corners and faces of {b} cubes?
test: {a} wants a sticker on each face, on each edge and on each corner of {b} cube boxes. How many stickers does {a.he} need?
exercise: How many faces, edges and corners are there altogether on {b} cubes?
exercise: {a} in Florida stacks {b} cube-shaped blocks. What is the total number of their faces, edges and corners?
exercise: {b} cubes: how many faces, edges and corners in all?
exercise: {a} counts the faces, edges and corners of {b.words} cubes together. What total does {a.he} get?
exercise: A shop in London has {b} cube boxes. Add the faces, edges and corners of all the boxes together. How many is that?
exercise: Every cube has faces, edges and corners. How many of these are there combined on {b} cubes?
exercise: {a} in Perth puts a sticker on every face, every edge and every corner of {b} cubes. How many stickers does {a.he} use?
exercise: Find the total number of faces, edges and corners of {b} cubes.
test: {b} dice lie on a table in Dublin. How many faces, edges and corners do they have between them?
test: {a} from Quebec makes {b} cube frames with one stick per edge, one bead per corner and one card per face. How many sticks, beads and cards are used in all?
test: What do the corners, the faces and the edges of {b} cube-shaped boxes add up to?
test: Each of {b} ice cubes has faces, edges and corners. Count them all together. How many are there?
test: A cube has 8 corners. How many corners, edges and faces do {b} cubes have together?
test: {a} in Nevada has {b} sugar cubes and marks every corner, edge and face of each one. How many marks does {a.he} make?
exercise: {b} cubes, count faces edges n corners all together, how many
