exam: It is given that {a} possesses {b} boxes, each in the form of a cube. Determine the aggregate number of faces, edges and corners of the said boxes.
exam: Ascertain the sum of the numbers of faces, edges and vertices of {b.words} cubes taken together.
exam: Whereas a set comprises {b} cubes, state the total of all their faces, edges and corners.
exam: Compute the combined number of faces, edges and corners belonging to a collection of {b} cubical blocks.
exercise: The late Mr Hill left {a} {b} wooden cubes. How many faces, edges and corners do they have altogether?
exercise: {a}'s count was "below expectations": {a.he} counted only the faces. {a} has {b} cubes. How many faces, edges and corners do they really have in all?
